<LegalLayout title="Support - Ice Bath Timer: One Tap" description="Support and help for the Ice Bath Timer: One Tap iPhone and Apple Watch app.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Ice Bath Timer: One Tap</p>
  <h1>Support</h1>

  <p>Ice Bath Timer: One Tap is a simple timer for ice baths and cold plunges on Apple Watch. Tap the complication and the countdown starts at once. Your iPhone shows a calendar of the days you took a bath. There is no account and no setup.</p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h2>Do I need an account?</h2>
  <p>No. There is no sign-up and no login.</p>

  <h2>How do I start a bath?</h2>
  <p>Add the Ice Bath complication to your watch face, then tap it: the app opens and the get ready countdown starts straight away. You can also open the app and tap Start.</p>

  <h2>How do I change the bath length?</h2>
  <p>On your Apple Watch, swipe left from the Start page to Settings. Turn the Digital Crown to set Plunge (0:30 to 5:00) and Get ready (1 to 10 seconds). A change applies from your next bath.</p>

  <h2>What do the taps mean?</h2>
  <p>One tap on each countdown number, a stronger tap when the timer starts, a tap every 30 seconds during the bath, and a longer pattern of about 2 seconds when the bath is done.</p>

  <h2>Why does the Done screen say "HR unavailable"?</h2>
  <p>The app could not read enough heart rate during the bath. Check that Health access for Ice Bath is allowed (on your iPhone: Settings, Privacy &amp; Security, Health, Ice Bath) and that the Watch sits snugly on your wrist with nothing under it.</p>

  <h2>Can I stop a bath early?</h2>
  <p>There is no stop button. To abandon a bath, force quit the app. Nothing is recorded for that bath.</p>

  <h2>Why is my iPhone calendar empty?</h2>
  <p>The calendar fills from your Apple Watch: a drop appears on each day you finish a bath. If you have not finished a bath yet, or you do not use the app on an Apple Watch, the calendar stays empty.</p>

  <h2>Is my heart rate saved?</h2>
  <p>No. The app shows your heart rate during the bath and on the Done screen and does not keep it. The workout session it runs to measure heart rate is discarded at the end. See our <a href="/ice-bath/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>

  <h2>Need more help?</h2>
  <p>Email us at <a href="mailto:support@mikhailnarbekov.com">support@mikhailnarbekov.com</a>. We aim to reply within a few business days.</p>
</LegalLayout>
